Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Depends: python3 (>= 3.12), libvulkan1, libgomp1, libssl3 | libssl3t64
Provides: cherrycola
Replaces: cherrycola (<< 0.3.0)
Breaks: cherrycola (<< 0.3.0)
Recommends: python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-4.0, gir1.2-adw-1
Maintainer: GraceOS <https://github.com/itsHarshDabas/CherryColaLLM>
Homepage: https://github.com/itsHarshDabas/CherryColaLLM
Description: Run AI models on your own PC (llama.cpp built in, Ollama, LM Studio)
 CherryColaLLM is a command line tool and a GTK chat app for local models.
 It drives Ollama, llama.cpp's llama-server or LM Studio's server, with
 per-model load and sampling settings, every llama.cpp option,
 requantizing, and streaming models bigger than RAM from disk.
 llama.cpp (a Vulkan build that also runs on the CPU) comes with it, so
 .gguf files on this PC load right away; Ollama and LM Studio are optional.
 Nothing is downloaded until you ask for a model.
